  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mahesh Dattatray Kalkute vs The State Of Maharashtra on 23 September, 2021 Equivalent citations: Aironline 2021 Bom 3608 Author: Revati Mohite Dere Bench: Revati Mohite Dere 21. Digitally signed by Rupali Rajesh Rupali Wakodikar Rajesh Wakodikar Date: 2021.09.24 15:24:23 +0530 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Bail Application No. 3285 Of 2021 Mahesh Dattatray Kalkute ...Applica Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respond Mr. Rohan Hogle a/w Ms. Swarali Joglekar and Tushar Sonawne for Applicant. Ms. Anamika Malhotra, A.P.P for the Respondent-State. Coram : Revati Mohite Dere, J. Date : 23rd September, 2021",
    "facts": "2 By this application, the applicant seeks his enlarg in connection with C.R. No. 577 of 2021 registered with the Bho Station, Pune, for the alleged offences punishable under Sectio Mahesh Dattatray Kalkute vs The State Of Maharashtra on 23 September, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/156323686/ 1 273, 328 read with 34 of the Indian Penal Code and Section 30(2 Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. The allegations as against the Wakodikar 21. BA 3285-2021.d that he was found in possession of Vimal Pan Masala which is prohibited in Maharashtra as per the order of the Food Commissioner. The contraband which was found i.e. Vimal Pan Masala was valued at Rs. 1,10,440/-. Learned Counsel for the applicant submits that the co-accused in the said case, Gajanan Dnyanba Shinde has been released on bail and that the allegations as against Gajanan was that he had purchased the contraband from the applicant and was found selling the same. The contraband which was found with Gajanan was valued at Rs. 15,840/-. Learned Counsel for the applicant submits that taking the prosecution case as it stands, no offence under Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code is disclosed qua the applicant.",
